Let $h(i)$ be the probability of reaching state $3$ before state $0$. The boundary values are $h(0)=0$ and $h(3)=1$. <First-step analysis> at states $1$ and $2$ gives
$$
h(1)=\frac12h(2),
\qquad
h(2)=\frac12h(1)+\frac12.
$$
Therefore $h(1)=h(1)/4+1/4$, so the requested <hitting probability> is
$$
\boxed{h(1)=\frac13}.
$$

