Indeed, after substituting $p=n^{-2/3}\log n$, these terms are respectively
$$
O(n^{-1}(\log n)^{12}),\qquad
O(n^{-4/3}(\log n)^{11}),\qquad
O(n^{-1}(\log n)^9).
