The <first moment method> gives $\mathbb P(Y>0)\leq\mathbb EY\to0$. Part (i) says that $X\geq100$ with probability tending to one, so the <union bound> shows that, with probability tending to one, both $X\geq100$ and $Y=0$. On that event any one hundred of the $K_4$ copies are pairwise vertex-disjoint, proving <vertex-disjoint sparse clique copies> in this case.

