|\mathcal H_{\mathcal F_2}(x_{1:n})|
\leq(n+1)^m s(\mathcal G,n)^m.
$$
Taking the supremum over $x_{1:n}$ proves the general <growth bound for signs of m-term linear combinations>:
$$
\boxed{s(\mathcal H_{\mathcal F_2},n)
\leq(n+1)^m s(\mathcal G,n)^m.}
$$

